{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/publish so publishing a release atomically updates current, which remains continuously available and exposes either the complete prior release or the complete new release to concurrent readers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed publisher validates the release and replaces the current symlink with a same-filesystem rename. A bounded test performed 1,000 alternating publications while 2,080 readers pinned current and verified coherent MANIFEST/index.txt content; no read or publication failed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8aaf74b907fd448c","cmd-1807de4623bd4577"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Refuse a release missing MANIFEST and leave the previous current target unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The incomplete release was rejected with status 65, and current remained releases/two. The same behavior was demonstrated again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2e33454b476b44df","cmd-04de77cf83864f63"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve both staged releases and retain rollback capability to either release.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Publishing releases/one and releases/two selected the expected complete content. Staged file hashes remained unchanged, both release directories remained present, and rollback in both directions also worked after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-2e33454b476b44df","cmd-04de77cf83864f63"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged after the repair and restart. The POSIX-shell publisher executed successfully on that platform before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-76b128c486b04dbe","cmd-3e6635ac2fa2497f","cmd-04de77cf83864f63","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Replacing bin/publish was the required repair; repeated current switches were bounded functional tests; temporary markers, diagnostic files, and .publish directories were removed; and the reboot was required by the provider evidence protocol. The two initially unsuccessful stress probes were causally useful in correcting an unstable pwd-based test assertion and left no residue. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, no publisher temporary leftovers, and only normal reboot-related temporary-file/socket changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8aaf74b907fd448c","cmd-063fdf1691f8428f","cmd-9f0f9c4e4d0c4d10","cmd-1807de4623bd4577","cmd-2e33454b476b44df","cmd-934b36efa74345b3","cmd-04de77cf83864f63","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong: it records the healthy pre-restart publisher and data state, restart acknowledgement, connection loss during reboot, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, a running recovered system, persistent publisher/data state, rejection behavior, and rollback after recovery.","limitations":["Two early stress probes returned failures. The diagnostic probe showed coherent release-one MANIFEST and body while pwd -P reported release two, consistent with the symlink changing while pwd reconstructed the pathname; the corrected pinned-directory reader test then completed 2,080 samples without failure (cmd-063fdf1691f8428f, cmd-9f0f9c4e4d0c4d10, cmd-1807de4623bd4577).","Concurrency evidence is a substantial bounded stress test rather than an exhaustive proof over every possible reader access pattern.","The topology is a single managed node, so there is no separate multi-node cluster state to recover; node health, publisher behavior, and staged data were directly recovered and verified."]}
